---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO } from "../consts";
---

<Base title="AI agents" description="Use tabnas to constrain LLM output, parse agent DSLs, and feed agent-consumable docs.">
  <h1>tabnas for AI agents</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Agents live and die by structure. tabnas gives you grammars as a first-class
    tool — to constrain what a model emits, to parse what it produces, and to
    make this documentation legible to the agents reading it.
  </p>

  <div class="tri">
    <article>
      <h2>Constrain output</h2>
      <p>Define the exact shape you expect back — a command, a query, a config —
        as a grammar, then parse the model's response. Malformed output fails
        loudly at a known position instead of silently corrupting downstream
        state.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Parse agent DSLs</h2>
      <p>Tool-call syntaxes, planning notations, and mini-languages are just
        grammars. Describe one once and parse it identically in your TypeScript
        orchestrator and your Go runtime.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Agent-consumable docs</h2>
      <p>This site publishes an <a href="/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a>
        index and clean, semantic docs so coding agents can ingest tabnas
        directly — no scraping guesswork.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>Roadmap</h2>
  <p>
    Coming next: machine-readable grammar catalogs and an MCP server so an agent
    can discover and use tabnas grammars as tools. Track progress on
    <a href={REPO("parser")} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> — and tell
    us what you'd want from an agent integration.
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede { font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 62ch; }
  .tri { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.25rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
  .tri article { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 1.25rem; background: var(--surface); }
  .tri h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .tri p { color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .tri { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
